This study also contributes to the literature on RK designs. %
\citet{card2015ecta} propose the RK design to identify a local average treatment effect in the absence of an instrument. \citet{cs2019} propose a quantile RK ($\mathrm{QRK}$) estimand to discover the heterogeneity of causal effects in the RK design with continuous treatment. %
In the context of binary treatment,
\citet{dong2018} considers a local average treatment effect quantity  that differs from that of \citet{card2015ecta}; \citet{ccs2020} consider the identification and estimation of a local quantile treatment effect; \citet{chenFan2019} examine the identification and local wavelet estimation of a weighted average treatment effect. %
