    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{images/fig2_merged.pdf}
    \caption{ {\bf Band inversions.} (a-d) Evolution of minibands at the K-valley as the SAW wavelength is varied for $m=20$~meV and $P = 1$~W/m. Minibands are labeled with their valley Chern number. For small wavelengths, the conduction and valence minibands around the charge neutrality point $E=0$ have zero Chern number. As $\lambda$ is increased a band inversion occurs at the Dirac point. Further increase of $\lambda$ results in a second band inversion at the M-point. (e) Berry curvature at $\lambda = 66\ \mathrm{nm}$ is highly concentrated at $\Gamma$ and $M$.}
