Once a block has been rewritten, we verify that the modified IR is functionally identical to its original form. To achieve this, both the original and transformed IR are converted into structured formats and compared at the component level. This verification process inspects variables, memory addresses, constants, and overall structure to ensure semantic consistency. If any mismatch is detected, the block is flagged for further inspection or discarded from the optimization pool.


