\begin{abstract}
  We address the problem of local type inference for a language based on System
  F with context-free session types. We present an algorithm that leverages the
  bidirectional type checking approach to propagate type information, enabling
  first class polymorphism while addressing the intricacies brought about by the
  sequential composition operator and type equivalence. The algorithm improves
  the language's usability by eliminating the need for type annotations at type
  application sites.
\end{abstract}


